{
  "dom_id": "step-q25571",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "The value of a new sewing machine is $\\$640.$ If the machine's value depreciates by one half every year, what will be its value after three years?",
  "worked_solution": "The initial value is $640$ dollars, and its value reduces by $\\frac{1}{2}$ every year.\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, the value will be $640\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2})$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, the value will be $640\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, the value will be $640\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}$ dollars.\n\nEvaluating the last expression, we get\n\n$$\n640\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}=80.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sewing machine will be worth $\\$80$ after $3$ years.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
